    "id": "p19-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Solve this equation.\n$$\\frac{7}{4}=1+\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{1}{x}}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=3$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{4}&=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{1}{x}}\\\\\\frac{3}{4}\\left(1+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)&=1\\\\1+\\frac{1}{x}&=\\frac{4}{3}\\\\\\frac{1}{x}&=\\frac{1}{3}\\\\3&=x\\end{align*}$$\nThe restrictions are $x\\ne0,-1$; $x=3$ is valid.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
